---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About - Flagswitch"
  description="Flagswitch is an open-source feature flag platform built for developers who want to ship without fear."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="pt-14 sm:pt-16">
    <section class="py-16 sm:py-20 md:py-28">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl w-full px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">

        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-brand-600 dark:text-brand-400 text-center">About</p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-white sm:text-4xl leading-snug text-center">
          We got tired of redeploying<br />just to turn a feature off.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-5 text-base sm:text-lg text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Every team hits the same wall. You ship a feature, something goes wrong, and turning it off means a hotfix, a
          review, and a deploy at 11pm. Or you're sitting on a half-done feature behind an env var that three people
          have to remember exists. That's the mess Flagswitch was built to clean up.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-12 border-t border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 pt-10">

          <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
            <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-700 bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900/70 p-6">
              <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">The problem</h2>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
                Feature control shouldn't require a deployment. But without proper tooling, that's exactly what it does.
                Env vars get forgotten, rollbacks are slow, and there's no single place to see what's on or off in production.
                Small teams feel this the most — there's no internal platform team to build the right solution.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-700 bg-white dark:bg-zinc-900/70 p-6">
              <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">Our bet</h2>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
                One SDK, one dashboard, and a flag that takes seconds to flip. No infra to manage, no enterprise contract
                to sign. Wrap a flag around any feature, control it remotely, and ship knowing you have an off switch.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4">
            <div class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-700 bg-zinc-50 dark:bg-zinc-900/60 p-6">
              <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">Open source</h2>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
                The code is open. Read it, fork it, or contribute. The infrastructure your product relies on shouldn't be
                a black box.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
